  "prefLabel": "He-P 2702.09 Inspection of Dairy Farms",
  "priorExpiration": "2008-12-28",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "He-P 2702.09 Inspection of Dairy Farms.\n\n(a) Inspections of all milk producers shall be conducted in accordance with RSA 184:82, RSA 184:92, and Mil 301.\n\n(b) Inspections shall be conducted:\n\n(1) Prior to issuance of a producer permit;\n\n(2) At least twice each year in accordance with RSA 184:92; and\n\n(3) Whenever the department has reason to believe a condition exists that places the producer in non-compliance with Mil 301, RSA 184, or He-P 2700.\n\n(c) When violations of critical item are found during an inspection, the department shall conduct a follow-up inspection.\n\n(d) When only non-critical violations are found during an inspection, the next inspection shall take place within 6 months.\n\n(e) If any item is debited 3 consecutive times, a warning letter shall be issued to the milk producer informing them that their producer permit shall be suspended unless one of the following is complied with:\n\n(1) An inspection conducted by the department showing the item or items outlined in the warning letter have been corrected. This inspection shall occur within 21 days from the date of this letter but not before the lapse of 3 days; or\n\n(2) The producer enters into a compliance agreement with the department to correct the item or items outlined in the warning letter prior to the producer permit being suspended.\n\nSource. #7315, eff 7-1-00; ss by #9189, INTERIM, eff 7-1-08, EXPIRES: 12-28-08; ss by #9325, eff 11-21-08; ss by #12101, eff 2-3-17; ss by #13175, eff 3-2-21",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/he-p2700.html"
